IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg7-governing-provisions`
IMPORT `dg7-appraisal-rights`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, s 262(d), (e), (f) -- APPRAISAL RIGHTS: HOW THEY ARE PERFECTED, AND THE PETITION.
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text); `-- src:N | ...` quotes line N.
--
-- Subsection (d) says how a stockholder perfects appraisal rights: notice to the stockholders (paragraph (1) before a meeting;
-- paragraph (2) where the transaction was approved by consent under s 228 or under s 251(h), s 253 or s 267), the stockholder's
-- written demand, and (paragraph (3)) a beneficial owner's own demand. Subsection (e) fixes the 120-day and 60-day periods and
-- the stockholder's right to a statement of numbers. Subsection (f) is the verified list that the surviving, resulting or
-- converted entity files in the Court of Chancery.
--
-- Every time limit is read with the last day INSIDE the period, and "before" as strictly before (fork F-d1, in NOTES.md).
-- Duties and conditions are BOOLEAN, DATE or NUMBER rules, not DEONTIC rules: a rule can then be asserted, and a seat layer
-- can export it.
-- OUT OF RANGE (plain inputs): s 255(c) (notice to members of a nonstock constituent: piece dg7, dg7-nonstock-mergers.l4),
-- s 251(h) (the offer, "consummation", "excluded stock": piece dg6), s 228 (consent: piece dg5), s 114 (nonstock corporations:
-- piece dg1), s 262(a) to (c) (this piece, dg7-appraisal-rights.l4), the verified list's "agreements as to value" (a fact).

§ `s 262(d) Shared building blocks`

-- How a stockholder's demand reaches the corporation or the entity: in writing, or by electronic transmission "if directed to
-- an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in such notice".
-- src:1264 | Each stockholder electing to demand the appraisal of such stockholder’s shares shall deliver to the corporation, before the taking of the vote on the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, a written demand for appraisal of such stockholder’s shares; provided that a demand may be delivered to the corporation by electronic transmission if directed to an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in such notice …
-- src:1265 | Any stockholder entitled to appraisal rights may, within 20 days after the date of giving such notice or, in the case of a merger approved pursuant to § 251(h) of this title, within the later of the consummation of the offer contemplated by § 251(h) of this title and 20 days after the date of giving such notice, demand in writing from the surviving, resulting or converted entity the appraisal of such holder’s shares; provided that a demand may be delivered to such entity by electronic transmission if directed to an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in such notice …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264); § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
DECLARE `s 262(d) How the demand was delivered` IS ONE OF
    `in writing, not by electronic transmission`
    `by electronic transmission directed to an information processing system expressly designated for that purpose in the notice`
    `by electronic transmission not so directed`

-- src:1264 | Each stockholder electing to demand the appraisal of such stockholder’s shares shall deliver to the corporation, before the taking of the vote on the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, a written demand for appraisal of such stockholder’s shares; provided that a demand may be delivered to the corporation by electronic transmission if directed to an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in such notice …
-- src:1265 | Any stockholder entitled to appraisal rights may, within 20 days after the date of giving such notice or, in the case of a merger approved pursuant to § 251(h) of this title, within the later of the consummation of the offer contemplated by § 251(h) of this title and 20 days after the date of giving such notice, demand in writing from the surviving, resulting or converted entity the appraisal of such holder’s shares; provided that a demand may be delivered to such entity by electronic transmission if directed to an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in such notice …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264); § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN h IS A `s 262(d) How the demand was delivered`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d) the demand was delivered in a way the subsection allows` h MEANS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `in writing, not by electronic transmission`                                                                                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `by electronic transmission directed to an information processing system expressly designated for that purpose in the notice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `by electronic transmission not so directed`                                                                                THEN FALSE

-- "Such demand will be sufficient if it reasonably informs the corporation [entity] of the identity of the stockholder and that
-- the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of such stockholder's shares."
-- src:1264 | Such demand will be sufficient if it reasonably informs the corporation of the identity of the stockholder and that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN `the demand reasonably informs the recipient of the identity of the stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand reasonably informs the recipient that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d) the demand is sufficient in what it says` `the demand reasonably informs the recipient of the identity of the stockholder` `the demand reasonably informs the recipient that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of the shares` MEANS
        `the demand reasonably informs the recipient of the identity of the stockholder`
    AND `the demand reasonably informs the recipient that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of the shares`

-- What a notice of appraisal rights contains. Paragraph (1) asks for a statement that appraisal rights are available and either
-- a copy of s 262 (and of s 114 if a constituent or the converting corporation is a nonstock corporation) or information
-- directing the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource where the section (and s 114, if applicable)
-- may be accessed without subscription or cost. Paragraph (2) adds a statement of the approval and, if the notice is given
-- on or after the effective date, of the effective date.
-- src:1264 | that appraisal rights are available for any or all of the shares of the constituent corporations or the converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation, and shall include in such notice either a copy of this section (and, if 1 of the constituent corporations or the converting corporation is a nonstock corporation, a copy of § 114 of this title) or information directing the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource at which this section (and, § 114 of this title, if applicable) may be accessed without subscription or cost …
-- src:1265 | of the approval of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance and that appraisal rights are available for any or all shares of such class or series of stock of such constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation, and shall include in such notice either a copy of this section (and, if 1 of the constituent corporations or the converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation is a nonstock corporation, a copy of § 114 of this title) or information directing the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource at which this section (and § 114 of this title, if applicable) may be accessed without subscription or cost …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264); § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
DECLARE `s 262(d) Notice of appraisal rights` HAS
    `states that appraisal rights are available for any or all of the shares`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `states that the transaction has been approved`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN   -- paragraph (2) only
    `includes a copy of s 262`                                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `includes a copy of s 114`                                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `directs the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource where s 262 may be accessed without subscription or cost` IS A BOOLEAN
    `directs the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource where s 114 may be accessed without subscription or cost` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the effective date of the transaction`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN

-- "if 1 of the constituent corporations or the converting corporation is a nonstock corporation": the kinds of the corporations
-- that are constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing.
-- src:1264 | and shall include in such notice either a copy of this section (and, if 1 of the constituent corporations or the converting corporation is a nonstock corporation, a copy of § 114 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN kinds IS A LIST OF `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d) one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation` kinds MEANS
    any `the kind is a nonstock corporation` kinds

-- src:1264 | and shall include in such notice either a copy of this section (and, if 1 of the constituent corporations or the converting corporation is a nonstock corporation, a copy of § 114 of this title) or information directing the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource at which this section (and, § 114 of this title, if applicable) may be accessed without subscription or cost …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN n IS A `s 262(d) Notice of appraisal rights`
      `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d) the notice offers s 262 and, if one of the corporations is nonstock, s 114` n `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation` MEANS
        (       n's `includes a copy of s 262`
          AND (   (NOT `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation`)
               OR n's `includes a copy of s 114`))
     OR (       n's `directs the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource where s 262 may be accessed without subscription or cost`
          AND (   (NOT `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation`)
               OR n's `directs the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource where s 114 may be accessed without subscription or cost`))

§ `s 262(d)(1) Notice before a meeting, and the demand`

-- Paragraph (1) governs where the transaction "is to be submitted for approval at a meeting of stockholders"; paragraph (2)
-- where it "was approved pursuant to s 228, s 251(h), s 253, or s 267".
-- src:1264 | (1) If a proposed merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance for which appraisal rights are provided under this section is to be submitted for approval at a meeting of stockholders …
-- src:1265 | (2) If the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance was approved pursuant to § 228, § 251(h), § 253, or § 267 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264); § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN a IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(1) paragraph (1) governs the transaction` a MEANS
    a EQUALS `approved at a meeting of stockholders`

-- src:1265 | (2) If the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance was approved pursuant to § 228, § 251(h), § 253, or § 267 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN a IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(2) paragraph (2) governs the transaction` a MEANS
        a EQUALS `approved by consent of stockholders pursuant to s 228`
    OR a EQUALS `approved pursuant to s 251(h)`
    OR a EQUALS `approved pursuant to s 253`
    OR a EQUALS `approved pursuant to s 267`

-- "the corporation, not less than 20 days prior to the meeting, shall notify each of its stockholders": the last day for the notice
-- is the day 20 days before the meeting (fork F-d1: the 20th day before is inside the period).
-- src:1264 | the corporation, not less than 20 days prior to the meeting, shall notify each of its stockholders who was such on the record date for notice of such meeting …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 262(d)(1) the latest date for the corporation's notice of the meeting` `the date of the meeting` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 20) `before` `the date of the meeting`

-- src:1264 | the corporation, not less than 20 days prior to the meeting, shall notify each of its stockholders who was such on the record date for notice of such meeting …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(1) the corporation's notice was given in time` `the date the notice was given` `the date of the meeting` MEANS
    `the date the notice was given` AT MOST `s 262(d)(1) the latest date for the corporation's notice of the meeting` `the date of the meeting`

-- Who is owed the notice: "each of its stockholders who was such on the record date for notice of such meeting (or such
-- members who received notice in accordance with s 255(c) of this title) with respect to shares for which appraisal rights
-- are available pursuant to subsection (b) or (c)". Appraisal rights being available is decided by
-- `s 262 appraisal rights are available for the shares` (dg7-appraisal-rights.l4).
-- src:1264 | shall notify each of its stockholders who was such on the record date for notice of such meeting (or such members who received notice in accordance with § 255(c) of this title) with respect to shares for which appraisal rights are available pursuant to subsection (b) or (c) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN `the person was a stockholder on the record date for notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member who received notice in accordance with s 255(c)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 255(c) is encoded in dg7-nonstock-mergers.l4
      `appraisal rights are available for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(1) the corporation must notify the person of the availability of appraisal rights` `the person was a stockholder on the record date for notice of the meeting` `the person is a member who received notice in accordance with s 255(c)` `appraisal rights are available for the shares` MEANS
        (   `the person was a stockholder on the record date for notice of the meeting`
         OR `the person is a member who received notice in accordance with s 255(c)`)
    AND `appraisal rights are available for the shares`

-- The contents of the notice: a statement that appraisal rights are available, and s 262 (with s 114) or the electronic resource.
-- src:1264 | that appraisal rights are available for any or all of the shares of the constituent corporations or the converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation, and shall include in such notice either a copy of this section (and, if 1 of the constituent corporations or the converting corporation is a nonstock corporation, a copy of § 114 of this title) or information directing the stockholders to a publicly available electronic resource at which this section (and, § 114 of this title, if applicable) may be accessed without subscription or cost …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN n IS A `s 262(d) Notice of appraisal rights`
      `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(1) the notice has the contents the paragraph requires` n `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation` MEANS
        n's `states that appraisal rights are available for any or all of the shares`
    AND `s 262(d) the notice offers s 262 and, if one of the corporations is nonstock, s 114` n `one of the corporations is a nonstock corporation`

-- The stockholder's demand, paragraph (1): delivered "before the taking of the vote", in writing (or to the designated system),
-- sufficient in what it says, and "by a separate written demand": "A proxy or vote against the merger ... shall not constitute
-- such a demand." The text gives no clock time for "before the taking of the vote", so that is one fact.
-- src:1264 | Each stockholder electing to demand the appraisal of such stockholder’s shares shall deliver to the corporation, before the taking of the vote on the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, a written demand for appraisal of such stockholder’s shares; provided that a demand may be delivered to the corporation by electronic transmission if directed to an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in such notice. Such demand will be sufficient if it reasonably informs the corporation of the identity of the stockholder and that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of such stockholder’s shares. A proxy or vote against the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance shall not constitute such a demand. A stockholder electing to take such action must do so by a separate written demand as herein provided. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
DECLARE `s 262(d)(1) Demand before the vote` HAS
    `delivered to the corporation before the taking of the vote`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `how the demand was delivered`                                                                 IS A `s 262(d) How the demand was delivered`
    `the demand reasonably informs the corporation of the identity of the stockholder`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand reasonably informs the corporation that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of the stockholder's shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand is a separate written demand and not merely a proxy or a vote against the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1264 | Each stockholder electing to demand the appraisal of such stockholder’s shares shall deliver to the corporation, before the taking of the vote on the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, a written demand for appraisal of such stockholder’s shares; provided that a demand may be delivered to the corporation by electronic transmission if directed to an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in such notice. Such demand will be sufficient if it reasonably informs the corporation of the identity of the stockholder and that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of such stockholder’s shares. A proxy or vote against the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance shall not constitute such a demand. A stockholder electing to take such action must do so by a separate written demand as herein provided. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN d IS A `s 262(d)(1) Demand before the vote`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(1) the stockholder's demand is good` d MEANS
        d's `delivered to the corporation before the taking of the vote`
    AND `s 262(d) the demand was delivered in a way the subsection allows` (d's `how the demand was delivered`)
    AND `s 262(d) the demand is sufficient in what it says` (d's `the demand reasonably informs the corporation of the identity of the stockholder`) (d's `the demand reasonably informs the corporation that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of the stockholder's shares`)
    AND d's `the demand is a separate written demand and not merely a proxy or a vote against the transaction`

-- "Within 10 days after the effective date ..., the surviving, resulting or converted entity shall notify each stockholder ... who
-- has complied with this subsection and has not voted in favor of or consented to the [transaction], and any beneficial owner who
-- has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3), of the date that the [transaction] has become effective".
-- src:1264 | Within 10 days after the effective date of such merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, the surviving, resulting or converted entity shall notify each stockholder of each constituent or converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation who has complied with this subsection and has not voted in favor of or consented to the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, and any beneficial owner who has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3) of this section, of the date that the merger, consolidation or conversion has become effective; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 262(d)(1) the latest date for the notice of the effective date` `the effective date` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 10) `after` `the effective date`

-- src:1264 | Within 10 days after the effective date of such merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, the surviving, resulting or converted entity shall notify each stockholder of each constituent or converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation who has complied with this subsection and has not voted in favor of or consented to the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, and any beneficial owner who has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3) of this section, of the date that the merger, consolidation or conversion has become effective; or
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN `the date the notice of the effective date was given` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(1) the notice of the effective date was given in time` `the date the notice of the effective date was given` `the effective date` MEANS
    `the date the notice of the effective date was given` AT MOST `s 262(d)(1) the latest date for the notice of the effective date` `the effective date`

-- src:1264 | shall notify each stockholder of each constituent or converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation who has complied with this subsection and has not voted in favor of or consented to the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, and any beneficial owner who has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(1) (src:1264)
GIVEN `the person has complied with subsection (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person voted in favor of or consented to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a beneficial owner who has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(1) the entity must notify the person of the date the transaction became effective` `the person has complied with subsection (d)` `the person voted in favor of or consented to the transaction` `the person is a beneficial owner who has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3)` MEANS
        (       `the person has complied with subsection (d)`
          AND (NOT `the person voted in favor of or consented to the transaction`))
     OR `the person is a beneficial owner who has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3)`

§ `s 262(d)(2) Notice after the transaction was approved without a meeting, and the demand`

-- Who gives the first notice, and when: "either a constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation
-- before the effective date ..., or the surviving, resulting or converted entity within 10 days after such effective date".
-- src:1265 | then either a constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation before the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, or the surviving, resulting or converted entity within 10 days after such effective date …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
DECLARE `s 262(d)(2) Who gives the notice` IS ONE OF
    `a constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation`
    `the surviving, resulting or converted entity`

-- src:1265 | then either a constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation before the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, or the surviving, resulting or converted entity within 10 days after such effective date …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN who IS A `s 262(d)(2) Who gives the notice`
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(2) the first notice was given in time` who `the date the notice was given` `the effective date` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `a constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation` THEN `the date the notice was given` LESS THAN `the effective date`
    WHEN `the surviving, resulting or converted entity`                                    THEN (       `the date the notice was given` AT LEAST `the effective date`
                                                                                                  AND `the date the notice was given` AT MOST `the date` (`period in days` 10) `after` `the effective date`)

-- The contents: notice of the approval, that appraisal rights are available, and s 262 (with s 114) or the electronic resource;
-- "Such notice may, and, if given on or after the effective date ..., shall, also notify such stockholders of the effective date."
