-- The later of two dates (used for the s 251(h) variants below).
GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 262(d)(2) the later of the two dates` a b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

-- "within 20 days after the date of giving such notice or, in the case of a merger approved pursuant to s 251(h), within the later
-- of the consummation of the offer contemplated by s 251(h) and 20 days after the date of giving such notice". The date of the
-- consummation of the offer is a fact of dg6's s 251(h); for a merger not approved under s 251(h) it is not asked.
-- NOTHING (not covered) if the merger was approved under s 251(h) and the consummation date is not given.
-- src:1265 | Any stockholder entitled to appraisal rights may, within 20 days after the date of giving such notice …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN a IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved`
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date the offer contemplated by s 251(h) was consummated` IS A MAYBE DATE   -- out of range: section 251(h), piece dg6
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 262(d)(2) the last day for the stockholder's demand` a `the date the notice was given` `the date the offer contemplated by s 251(h) was consummated` MEANS
    IF a EQUALS `approved pursuant to s 251(h)`
    THEN CONSIDER `the date the offer contemplated by s 251(h) was consummated`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST consummation THEN JUST (`s 262(d)(2) the later of the two dates` consummation (`the date` (`period in days` 20) `after` `the date the notice was given`))
    ELSE JUST (`the date` (`period in days` 20) `after` `the date the notice was given`)

-- The demand under paragraph (2): "demand in writing from the surviving, resulting or converted entity", by the last day, and
-- sufficient in what it says. There is no separateness rule here as there is in paragraph (1).
-- src:1265 | Any stockholder entitled to appraisal rights may, within 20 days after the date of giving such notice or, in the case of a merger approved pursuant to § 251(h) of this title, within the later of the consummation of the offer contemplated by § 251(h) of this title and 20 days after the date of giving such notice, demand in writing from the surviving, resulting or converted entity the appraisal of such holder’s shares; provided that a demand may be delivered to such entity by electronic transmission if directed to an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in such notice. Such demand will be sufficient if it reasonably informs such entity of the identity of the stockholder and that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of such holder’s shares. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
DECLARE `s 262(d)(2) Demand after the notice` HAS
    `the date the demand was delivered`                                                             IS A DATE
    `how the demand was delivered`                                                                  IS A `s 262(d) How the demand was delivered`
    `the demand reasonably informs the entity of the identity of the stockholder`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand reasonably informs the entity that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of the holder's shares` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1265 | Any stockholder entitled to appraisal rights may, within 20 days after the date of giving such notice or, in the case of a merger approved pursuant to § 251(h) of this title, within the later of the consummation of the offer contemplated by § 251(h) of this title and 20 days after the date of giving such notice, demand in writing from the surviving, resulting or converted entity the appraisal of such holder’s shares; provided that a demand may be delivered to such entity by electronic transmission if directed to an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in such notice. Such demand will be sufficient if it reasonably informs such entity of the identity of the stockholder and that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of such holder’s shares. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN d IS A `s 262(d)(2) Demand after the notice`
      `the last day for the demand` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(2) the stockholder's demand is good` d `the last day for the demand` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day for the demand`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN JUST (
                (d's `the date the demand was delivered` AT MOST lastDay)
            AND `s 262(d) the demand was delivered in a way the subsection allows` (d's `how the demand was delivered`)
            AND `s 262(d) the demand is sufficient in what it says` (d's `the demand reasonably informs the entity of the identity of the stockholder`) (d's `the demand reasonably informs the entity that the stockholder intends thereby to demand the appraisal of the holder's shares`))

-- The second notice. "If such notice did not notify stockholders of the effective date ..., either (i) each such constituent
-- corporation ... shall send a second notice before the effective date ... or (ii) the surviving, resulting or converted entity
-- shall send such a second notice to all such holders on or within 10 days after such effective date".
-- src:1265 | If such notice did not notify stockholders of the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, either (i) each such constituent corporation or the converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation shall send a second notice before the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance notifying each of the holders of any class or series of stock of such constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation that are entitled to appraisal rights of the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance or (ii) the surviving, resulting or converted entity shall send such a second notice to all such holders on or within 10 days after such effective date; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN `the first notice stated the effective date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(2) a second notice is required` `the first notice stated the effective date` MEANS
    NOT `the first notice stated the effective date`

-- src:1265 | If such notice did not notify stockholders of the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, either (i) each such constituent corporation or the converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation shall send a second notice before the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance notifying each of the holders of any class or series of stock of such constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation that are entitled to appraisal rights of the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance or (ii) the surviving, resulting or converted entity shall send such a second notice to all such holders on or within 10 days after such effective date; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN who IS A `s 262(d)(2) Who gives the notice`
      `the date the second notice was sent` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(2) the second notice was sent in time` who `the date the second notice was sent` `the effective date` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `a constituent, converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation` THEN `the date the second notice was sent` LESS THAN `the effective date`
    WHEN `the surviving, resulting or converted entity`                                    THEN (       `the date the second notice was sent` AT LEAST `the effective date`
                                                                                                  AND `the date the second notice was sent` AT MOST `the date` (`period in days` 10) `after` `the effective date`)

-- The proviso: "if such second notice is sent more than 20 days following the sending of the first notice or, in the case of a
-- merger approved pursuant to s 251(h), later than the later of the consummation of the offer ... and 20 days following the
-- sending of the first notice, such second notice need only be sent to each stockholder who is entitled to appraisal rights
-- and who has demanded appraisal ... and any beneficial owner who has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3)".
-- src:1265 | provided, however, that if such second notice is sent more than 20 days following the sending of the first notice …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN a IS A `s 262 How the transaction was approved`
      `the date the first notice was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date the offer contemplated by s 251(h) was consummated` IS A MAYBE DATE   -- out of range: section 251(h), piece dg6
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 262(d)(2) the last day on which the second notice must go to every holder entitled to appraisal rights` a `the date the first notice was sent` `the date the offer contemplated by s 251(h) was consummated` MEANS
    `s 262(d)(2) the last day for the stockholder's demand` a `the date the first notice was sent` `the date the offer contemplated by s 251(h) was consummated`

-- src:1265 | such second notice need only be sent to each stockholder who is entitled to appraisal rights and who has demanded appraisal of such holder’s shares in accordance with this subsection and any beneficial owner who has demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN `the date the second notice was sent` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the second notice must go to every holder` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the holder is entitled to appraisal rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder has demanded appraisal in accordance with paragraph (d)(2) or is a beneficial owner who has demanded under paragraph (d)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(2) the second notice must be sent to the holder` `the date the second notice was sent` `the last day on which the second notice must go to every holder` `the holder is entitled to appraisal rights` `the holder has demanded appraisal in accordance with paragraph (d)(2) or is a beneficial owner who has demanded under paragraph (d)(3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day on which the second notice must go to every holder`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN JUST (
        IF `the date the second notice was sent` AT MOST lastDay
        THEN `the holder is entitled to appraisal rights`
        ELSE (       `the holder is entitled to appraisal rights`
               AND `the holder has demanded appraisal in accordance with paragraph (d)(2) or is a beneficial owner who has demanded under paragraph (d)(3)`))

-- The affidavit. "An affidavit of the secretary or assistant secretary or of the transfer agent of the corporation or entity that
-- is required to give either notice that such notice has been given shall, in the absence of fraud, be prima facie evidence of
-- the facts stated therein."
-- src:1265 | An affidavit of the secretary or assistant secretary or of the transfer agent of the corporation or entity that is required to give either notice that such notice has been given shall, in the absence of fraud, be prima facie evidence of the facts stated therein …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
DECLARE `s 262(d)(2) Who made the affidavit` IS ONE OF
    `the secretary of the corporation or entity`
    `the assistant secretary of the corporation or entity`
    `the transfer agent of the corporation or entity`
    `someone else`

-- src:1265 | An affidavit of the secretary or assistant secretary or of the transfer agent of the corporation or entity that is required to give either notice that such notice has been given shall, in the absence of fraud, be prima facie evidence of the facts stated therein …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN who IS A `s 262(d)(2) Who made the affidavit`
      `the corporation or entity is required to give the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit says that the notice has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was fraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(2) the affidavit is prima facie evidence that the notice was given` who `the corporation or entity is required to give the notice` `the affidavit says that the notice has been given` `there was fraud` MEANS
        (   who EQUALS `the secretary of the corporation or entity`
         OR who EQUALS `the assistant secretary of the corporation or entity`
         OR who EQUALS `the transfer agent of the corporation or entity`)
    AND `the corporation or entity is required to give the notice`
    AND `the affidavit says that the notice has been given`
    AND (NOT `there was fraud`)

-- The record date for the notices. The corporation "may fix, in advance, a record date that shall be not more than 10 days prior to
-- the date the notice is given, provided, that if the notice is given on or after the effective date ..., the record date shall be
-- such effective date. If no record date is fixed and the notice is given prior to the effective date, the record date shall be
-- the close of business on the day next preceding the day on which the notice is given."
-- Not covered (NOTHING): a record date that the corporation fixed before the effective date but that is more than 10 days before the
-- notice, or after it; the text says what the record date "shall" be only for the cases above.
-- src:1265 | For purposes of determining the stockholders entitled to receive either notice, each constituent corporation or the converting, transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation may fix, in advance, a record date that shall be not more than 10 days prior to the date the notice is given, provided, that if the notice is given on or after the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, the record date shall be such effective date. If no record date is fixed and the notice is given prior to the effective date, the record date shall be the close of business on the day next preceding the day on which the notice is given …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(2) (src:1265)
GIVEN `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
      `the record date the corporation fixed in advance` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 262(d)(2) the record date for the notice` `the date the notice was given` `the effective date` `the record date the corporation fixed in advance` MEANS
    IF `the date the notice was given` AT LEAST `the effective date`
    THEN JUST `the effective date`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the record date the corporation fixed in advance`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`the date the notice was given` MINUS 1)
         WHEN JUST fixed THEN IF   fixed AT MOST `the date the notice was given`
                                   AND fixed AT LEAST `the date` (`period in days` 10) `before` `the date the notice was given`
                              THEN JUST fixed
                              ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 262(d)(3) A beneficial owner's own demand`

-- A beneficial owner "may, in such person's name, demand in writing an appraisal of such beneficial owner's shares in accordance
-- with either paragraph (d)(1) or (2) ..., as applicable; provided that (i) such beneficial owner continuously owns such shares
-- through the effective date ... and otherwise satisfies the requirements applicable to a stockholder under the first sentence of
-- subsection (a) ... and (ii) the demand ... reasonably identifies the holder of record of the shares for which the demand is made,
-- is accompanied by documentary evidence of such beneficial owner's beneficial ownership of stock and a statement that such
-- documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be, and provides an address at which such beneficial
-- owner consents to receive notices given by the surviving, resulting or converted entity hereunder and to be set forth on the
-- verified list required by subsection (f)".
-- Limb (i) is read through `s 262(a) the claimant meets the conditions of the first sentence other than holding of record`, which
-- already asks for continuous holding through the effective date.
-- src:1266 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (a) of this section (but subject to this paragraph (d)(3)), a beneficial owner may, in such person’s name, demand in writing an appraisal of such beneficial owner’s shares in accordance with either paragraph (d)(1) or (2) of this section, as applicable; provided that (i) such beneficial owner continuously owns such shares through the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance and otherwise satisfies the requirements applicable to a stockholder under the first sentence of subsection (a) of this section and (ii) the demand made by such beneficial owner reasonably identifies the holder of record of the shares for which the demand is made, is accompanied by documentary evidence of such beneficial owner’s beneficial ownership of stock and a statement that such documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be, and provides an address at which such beneficial owner consents to receive notices given by the surviving, resulting or converted entity hereunder and to be set forth on the verified list required by subsection (f) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(3) (src:1266)
DECLARE `s 262(d)(3) The beneficial owner's demand` HAS
    `the demand is made in writing in the beneficial owner's name in accordance with paragraph (d)(1) or (2), as applicable`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand reasonably identifies the holder of record of the shares for which the demand is made`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand is accompanied by documentary evidence of the beneficial owner's beneficial ownership of stock`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand is accompanied by a statement that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the demand provides an address at which the beneficial owner consents to receive notices and to be set forth on the verified list` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1266 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (a) of this section (but subject to this paragraph (d)(3)), a beneficial owner may, in such person’s name, demand in writing an appraisal of such beneficial owner’s shares in accordance with either paragraph (d)(1) or (2) of this section, as applicable; provided that (i) such beneficial owner continuously owns such shares through the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance and otherwise satisfies the requirements applicable to a stockholder under the first sentence of subsection (a) of this section and (ii) the demand made by such beneficial owner reasonably identifies the holder of record of the shares for which the demand is made, is accompanied by documentary evidence of such beneficial owner’s beneficial ownership of stock and a statement that such documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be, and provides an address at which such beneficial owner consents to receive notices given by the surviving, resulting or converted entity hereunder and to be set forth on the verified list required by subsection (f) of this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(d)(3) (src:1266)
GIVEN `the person is a beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A `s 262(a) Claimant`
      d IS A `s 262(d)(3) The beneficial owner's demand`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(d)(3) the beneficial owner's demand is good` `the person is a beneficial owner` c d MEANS
        `the person is a beneficial owner`
    AND d's `the demand is made in writing in the beneficial owner's name in accordance with paragraph (d)(1) or (2), as applicable`
    AND `s 262(a) the claimant meets the conditions of the first sentence other than holding of record` c
    AND d's `the demand reasonably identifies the holder of record of the shares for which the demand is made`
    AND d's `the demand is accompanied by documentary evidence of the beneficial owner's beneficial ownership of stock`
    AND d's `the demand is accompanied by a statement that the documentary evidence is a true and correct copy of what it purports to be`
    AND d's `the demand provides an address at which the beneficial owner consents to receive notices and to be set forth on the verified list`

§ `s 262(e) The petition, withdrawal and the statement of numbers`

-- "Within 120 days after the effective date of the merger ..., the surviving, resulting or converted entity, or any person who
-- has complied with subsections (a) and (d) of this section and who is otherwise entitled to appraisal rights, may commence an
-- appraisal proceeding by filing a petition in the Court of Chancery". The 120th day is inside the period (fork F-d1).
-- src:1267 | (e) Within 120 days after the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, the surviving, resulting or converted entity, or any person who has complied with subsections (a) and (d) of this section and who is otherwise entitled to appraisal rights, may commence an appraisal proceeding by filing a petition in the Court of Chancery demanding a determination of the value of the stock of all such stockholders …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(e) (src:1267)
GIVEN `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 262(e) the last day for a petition` `the effective date` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 120) `after` `the effective date`

-- src:1267 | (e) Within 120 days after the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, the surviving, resulting or converted entity, or any person who has complied with subsections (a) and (d) of this section and who is otherwise entitled to appraisal rights, may commence an appraisal proceeding by filing a petition in the Court of Chancery demanding a determination of the value of the stock of all such stockholders …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(e) (src:1267)
GIVEN `the person is the surviving, resulting or converted entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has complied with subsections (a) and (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is otherwise entitled to appraisal rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the petition was filed` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(e) the person may commence an appraisal proceeding by this petition` `the person is the surviving, resulting or converted entity` `the person has complied with subsections (a) and (d)` `the person is otherwise entitled to appraisal rights` `the date the petition was filed` `the effective date` MEANS
        `the date the petition was filed` AT MOST `s 262(e) the last day for a petition` `the effective date`
    AND (   `the person is the surviving, resulting or converted entity`
         OR (       `the person has complied with subsections (a) and (d)`
              AND `the person is otherwise entitled to appraisal rights`))

-- "at any time within 60 days after the effective date ..., any person entitled to appraisal rights who has not commenced an
-- appraisal proceeding or joined that proceeding as a named party shall have the right to withdraw such person's demand for
-- appraisal and to accept the terms offered upon the [transaction]".
-- src:1267 | Notwithstanding the foregoing, at any time within 60 days after the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, any person entitled to appraisal rights who has not commenced an appraisal proceeding or joined that proceeding as a named party shall have the right to withdraw such person’s demand for appraisal and to accept the terms offered upon the merger …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(e) (src:1267)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to appraisal rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has commenced an appraisal proceeding or joined it as a named party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the withdrawal` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(e) the person may withdraw the demand and accept the terms offered` `the person is entitled to appraisal rights` `the person has commenced an appraisal proceeding or joined it as a named party` `the date of the withdrawal` `the effective date` MEANS
        `the person is entitled to appraisal rights`
    AND (NOT `the person has commenced an appraisal proceeding or joined it as a named party`)
    AND `the date of the withdrawal` AT MOST `the date` (`period in days` 60) `after` `the effective date`

-- The statement. "Within 120 days after the effective date ..., any person who has complied with the requirements of subsections
-- (a) and (d) ..., upon request given in writing (or by electronic transmission directed to an information processing system (if any)
-- expressly designated for that purpose in the notice of appraisal), shall be entitled to receive from the surviving, resulting or
-- converted entity a statement setting forth [the numbers below]".
-- src:1267 | Within 120 days after the effective date of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance, any person who has complied with the requirements of subsections (a) and (d) of this section, upon request given in writing (or by electronic transmission directed to an information processing system (if any) expressly designated for that purpose in the notice of appraisal), shall be entitled to receive from the surviving, resulting or converted entity a statement …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(e) (src:1267)
GIVEN `the person has complied with the requirements of subsections (a) and (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how the request was given` IS A `s 262(d) How the demand was delivered`
      `the date of the request` IS A DATE
      `the effective date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(e) the person is entitled to receive the statement` `the person has complied with the requirements of subsections (a) and (d)` `how the request was given` `the date of the request` `the effective date` MEANS
        `the person has complied with the requirements of subsections (a) and (d)`
    AND `s 262(d) the demand was delivered in a way the subsection allows` `how the request was given`
    AND `the date of the request` AT MOST `s 262(e) the last day for a petition` `the effective date`

-- "Such statement shall be given to the person within 10 days after such person's request for such a statement is received by the
-- surviving, resulting or converted entity or within 10 days after expiration of the period for delivery of demands for appraisal
-- under subsection (d) of this section, whichever is later."
-- src:1267 | Such statement shall be given to the person within 10 days after such person’s request for such a statement is received by the surviving, resulting or converted entity or within 10 days after expiration of the period for delivery of demands for appraisal under subsection (d) of this section, whichever is later …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(e) (src:1267)
GIVEN `the date the request was received` IS A DATE
      `the date the period for delivery of demands under subsection (d) expired` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 262(e) the last day for the statement` `the date the request was received` `the date the period for delivery of demands under subsection (d) expired` MEANS
    `s 262(d)(2) the later of the two dates` (`the date` (`period in days` 10) `after` `the date the request was received`) (`the date` (`period in days` 10) `after` `the date the period for delivery of demands under subsection (d) expired`)

-- src:1267 | Such statement shall be given to the person within 10 days after such person’s request for such a statement is received by the surviving, resulting or converted entity or within 10 days after expiration of the period for delivery of demands for appraisal under subsection (d) of this section, whichever is later …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(e) (src:1267)
GIVEN `the date the statement was given` IS A DATE
      `the date the request was received` IS A DATE
      `the date the period for delivery of demands under subsection (d) expired` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(e) the statement was given in time` `the date the statement was given` `the date the request was received` `the date the period for delivery of demands under subsection (d) expired` MEANS
    `the date the statement was given` AT MOST `s 262(e) the last day for the statement` `the date the request was received` `the date the period for delivery of demands under subsection (d) expired`

-- What the statement sets out. (1) "the aggregate number of shares not voted in favor of the [transaction]" or, for a merger approved
-- under s 251(h), "the aggregate number of shares (other than any excluded stock ...) that were the subject of, and were not tendered
-- into, and accepted for purchase or exchange in, the offer"; (2) "with respect to which demands for appraisal have been received";
-- (3) "the aggregate number of stockholders or beneficial owners holding or owning such shares (provided that, where a beneficial
-- owner makes a demand pursuant to paragraph (d)(3), the record holder of such shares shall not be considered a separate
-- stockholder holding such shares for purposes of such aggregate number)".
-- Reading F-e1: the shares counted for a s 251(h) merger are those that were the subject of the offer, less the excluded stock, less the shares
-- tendered into and accepted in the offer.
-- src:1267 | a statement setting forth the aggregate number of shares not voted in favor of the merger, consolidation, conversion, transfer, domestication or continuance (or, in the case of a merger approved pursuant to § 251(h) of this title, the aggregate number of shares (other than any excluded stock (as defined in § 251(h)(6)d. of this title)) that were the subject of, and were not tendered into, and accepted for purchase or exchange in, the offer …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(e) (src:1267)
GIVEN `the number of shares that were the subject of the offer` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those shares that were excluded stock` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those shares that were tendered into, and accepted for purchase or exchange in, the offer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 262(e) the number of shares the statement sets out for a s 251(h) merger` `the number of shares that were the subject of the offer` `the number of those shares that were excluded stock` `the number of those shares that were tendered into, and accepted for purchase or exchange in, the offer` MEANS
    (`the number of shares that were the subject of the offer` MINUS `the number of those shares that were excluded stock`) MINUS `the number of those shares that were tendered into, and accepted for purchase or exchange in, the offer`

-- src:1267 | and the aggregate number of stockholders or beneficial owners holding or owning such shares (provided that, where a beneficial owner makes a demand pursuant to paragraph (d)(3) of this section, the record holder of such shares shall not be considered a separate stockholder holding such shares for purposes of such aggregate number …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(e) (src:1267)
GIVEN `the number of record holders who demanded appraisal` IS A NUMBER
      `of those, the number whose shares are the subject of a beneficial owner's demand under paragraph (d)(3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of beneficial owners who demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 262(e) the aggregate number of stockholders or beneficial owners the statement sets out` `the number of record holders who demanded appraisal` `of those, the number whose shares are the subject of a beneficial owner's demand under paragraph (d)(3)` `the number of beneficial owners who demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3)` MEANS
    (`the number of record holders who demanded appraisal` MINUS `of those, the number whose shares are the subject of a beneficial owner's demand under paragraph (d)(3)`) PLUS `the number of beneficial owners who demanded appraisal under paragraph (d)(3)`

§ `s 262(f) The verified list`

-- "Upon the filing of any such petition by any person other than the surviving, resulting or converted entity, service of a copy
-- thereof shall be made upon such entity, which shall within 20 days after such service file in the office of the Register in
-- Chancery in which the petition was filed a duly verified list".
-- src:1268 | (f) Upon the filing of any such petition by any person other than the surviving, resulting or converted entity, service of a copy thereof shall be made upon such entity, which shall within 20 days after such service file in the office of the Register in Chancery in which the petition was filed a duly verified list …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(f) (src:1268)
GIVEN `the date of service of the petition on the entity` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 262(f) the last day for the entity to file the verified list` `the date of service of the petition on the entity` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 20) `after` `the date of service of the petition on the entity`

-- src:1268 | (f) Upon the filing of any such petition by any person other than the surviving, resulting or converted entity, service of a copy thereof shall be made upon such entity, which shall within 20 days after such service file in the office of the Register in Chancery in which the petition was filed a duly verified list …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(f) (src:1268)
GIVEN `the date the verified list was filed` IS A DATE
      `the date of service of the petition on the entity` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(f) the verified list was filed in time` `the date the verified list was filed` `the date of service of the petition on the entity` MEANS
    `the date the verified list was filed` AT MOST `s 262(f) the last day for the entity to file the verified list` `the date of service of the petition on the entity`

-- "If the petition shall be filed by the surviving, resulting or converted entity, the petition shall be accompanied by such a duly
-- verified list."
-- src:1268 | If the petition shall be filed by the surviving, resulting or converted entity, the petition shall be accompanied by such a duly verified list …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(f) (src:1268)
GIVEN `the petition is accompanied by a duly verified list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(f) the petition filed by the entity has the list it must have` `the petition is accompanied by a duly verified list` MEANS
    `the petition is accompanied by a duly verified list`

-- The list contains "the names and addresses of all persons who have demanded appraisal for their shares and with whom
-- agreements as to the value of their shares have not been reached by such entity".
-- src:1268 | a duly verified list containing the names and addresses of all persons who have demanded appraisal for their shares and with whom agreements as to the value of their shares have not been reached by such entity …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(f) (src:1268)
GIVEN `the person has demanded appraisal for the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement as to the value of the shares has been reached with the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(f) the person's name and address belong on the verified list` `the person has demanded appraisal for the shares` `an agreement as to the value of the shares has been reached with the entity` MEANS
        `the person has demanded appraisal for the shares`
    AND (NOT `an agreement as to the value of the shares has been reached with the entity`)

-- "The Register in Chancery, if so ordered by the Court, shall give notice of the time and place fixed for the hearing of such petition
-- by registered or certified mail to the surviving, resulting or converted entity and to the persons shown on the list at the
-- addresses therein stated." The Court's order is a judgment handed to the Court: a conditional input.
-- src:1268 | The Register in Chancery, if so ordered by the Court, shall give notice of the time and place fixed for the hearing of such petition by registered or certified mail to the surviving, resulting or converted entity and to the persons shown on the list at the addresses therein stated …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(f) (src:1268)
GIVEN `the person is shown on the list` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has ordered the Register in Chancery to give notice of the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 262(f) the person must be sent notice of the hearing by registered or certified mail at the address on the list` `the person is shown on the list` `the Court has ordered the Register in Chancery to give notice of the hearing` MEANS
        `the person is shown on the list`
    AND `the Court has ordered the Register in Chancery to give notice of the hearing`

-- "The forms of the notices by mail and by publication shall be approved by the Court, and the costs thereof shall be borne by the
-- surviving, resulting or converted entity." The party that bears the cost is the entity, not the person on the list.
-- src:1268 | The forms of the notices by mail and by publication shall be approved by the Court, and the costs thereof shall be borne by the surviving, resulting or converted entity …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 262(f) (src:1268)
GIVETH A Actor
`s 262(f) the party that bears the costs of the notices` MEANS
    `another party named in the provision` "the surviving, resulting or converted entity"
